{"id":"hotel-federal-reimbursement","title":"Federal reimbursement for the shelter hotels","question":"How much of the hotel programme has the federal emergency agency agreed to reimburse, according to its own records?","finding":"The federal emergency agency’s public file lists 42 coronavirus projects for the City with $305.7 million of federal money obligated; 4 of them are for shelter outside group settings, the heading hotel rooms fall under, with $62.1 million obligated. That is 21% of the $297.6 million the City paid on the room agreements alone. The analyst reported in July 2022 that “Approximately 91 percent of expenditures to date on Shelter in Place hotel agreements are eligible for reimbursement by the Federal Emergency Management Agency”. The shelter projects’ own titles cover 16 March 2020 to 30 June 2020; 23 January 2021 to 30 June 2022; none in the file covers 1 July 2020 to 22 January 2021. The City’s fiscal 2023 financial report says federal grant revenue fell $262.2 million short of budget mainly because the agency had put other jurisdictions’ claims first. The ledger shows $412.0 million received from the agency for all purposes from fiscal 2020 to 2026.","how":"OpenFEMA Public Assistance records for disaster 4482 (the coronavirus pandemic in California) where the applicant is the City and County of San Francisco: one row per project, with the project amount, the federal share obligated and any amount later taken back. A project is counted as shelter when the download’s flag for non-congregate shelter is set (its title carries the agency’s abbreviation for it). The ledger figure is the revenue line “FEMA - Federal Share” across all departments. Shelter projects are listed first.","limits":"An obligation is the agency’s commitment, not a payment, and the file is a snapshot: claims still under review or on appeal are not in it, which may explain much of the gap, and the City’s fiscal 2023 report says it expects more. The shelter projects also cover costs other than hotel rooms, and the hotel programme also drew on State and other federal money, which the analyst’s report lists. So the comparison brackets the answer and does not give it. What would settle it: the City’s own schedule of claims submitted to the agency for the hotel programme, with amounts approved, denied and pending, and the agency’s decisions on any appeal (the two second-appeal records on file give no text). Amounts, parties and dates taken from Board file titles are read by machine: in a hand check of 50 titles, 11 had at least one field read wrongly (4 after later fixes).","tier":"OFFICIAL","columns":[{"k":"project","t":"Project, as the agency titles it","type":"text"},{"k":"kind","t":"Kind","type":"text"},{"k":"amount","t":"Project amount","type":"usd"},{"k":"federal","t":"Federal share obligated","type":"usd"},{"k":"first","t":"First obligation","type":"date"},{"k":"last","t":"Latest obligation","type":"date"},{"k":"takenBack","t":"Later taken back","type":"usd"},{"k":"status","t":"Status","type":"text"}],"rows":[{"project":"SF County NCS 1/23/21-6/30/21","kind":"shelter outside group settings (hotel rooms and similar)","amount":54481394,"federal":54481394,"first":"2022-01-10","last":"2022-01-10","takenBack":null,"status":"Eligible; Pending Award"},{"project":"SF County NCS - 3/16/2020-6/30/2020 - #2","kind":"shelter outside group settings (hotel rooms and similar)","amount":7593690,"federal":7593690,"first":"2020-04-19","last":"2021-04-19","takenBack":null,"status":"Eligible; Pending Award"},{"project":"12.25.2021 through 6.30.2022 NCS","kind":"shelter outside group settings (hotel rooms and similar)","amount":29198,"federal":29198,"first":"2025-06-20","last":"2025-06-20","takenBack":null,"status":"Eligible; Project Closed Out"},{"project":"SF County NCS 7/1/21-12/24/2021","kind":"shelter outside group settings (hotel rooms and similar)","amount":11026,"federal":11026,"first":"2025-06-20","last":"2025-06-20","takenBack":null,"status":"Eli